# Use an access token belonging to user ID 1 for the post lifecycle requests below.
# The API determines the post owner from the token; it does not accept a user ID in the request body.
@postBookVolumeId = yow0EAAAQBAJ

### List all posts for the authenticated user (user ID 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Create a post for the authenticated user (user ID 1)
# @name createPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts/add/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "action": "post",
    "description": "Test post: created through test.http.",
    "id": "{{postBookVolumeId}}"
}

###

### Verify the created post
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Edit the created post
# @name updatePost
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/update/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "description": "Test post: updated through test.http."
}

###

### Verify the edited post
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Add a comment to the test post
# @name createComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/add_comment/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "text": "Test comment: added through test.http. --> var 2"
}

###

### List comments on the test post (includes the comment created above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/list_comments/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

# The API currently supports adding and listing comments, but has no comment update/delete routes.

### Check whether the authenticated user has liked the test post
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/has_liked/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Like the test post (toggle_like creates the like if it does not exist)
# @name likeTestPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/toggle_like/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Verify the like was added (expected: liked=true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/has_liked/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Unlike the test post (send toggle_like again to remove the like)
# @name unlikeTestPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/toggle_like/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Verify the like was removed (expected: liked=false)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/has_liked/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Delete the created post
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/delete/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###

### Verify the post was deleted (expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.id}}/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: JWT {{accessToken}}

###
